You are working in a Go repository checked out at /echo (module github.com/labstack/echo/v4, go1.16 toolchain). Fix a bug in /echo/context.go: `Scheme()` returns invalid forwarded-header values verbatim instead of ignoring them.

Apply EXACTLY this minimal edit to /echo/context.go (change nothing else, do NOT touch any test file):

In `func (c *context) Scheme() string`, replace the three guards that currently read `scheme != ""` with validity checks, so the function becomes:

```go
func (c *context) Scheme() string {
	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
	if c.IsTLS() {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	return "http"
}
```

(Keep the existing comment lines and the existing X-Forwarded-Ssl `== "on"` check exactly as they are; only the three `scheme != ""` conditions change.)

Then verify:
- `cd /echo && gofmt -l context.go` (must print nothing)
- `cd /echo && go build ./...`
- `cd /echo && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -30` — ALL pre-existing tests must still pass (especially TestContext_Scheme in context_test.go and the middleware tests).
- Write a TEMPORARY test file /echo/context_zz_tmp_test.go in package echo that reproduces the hidden expectations:
  * `X-Forwarded-Proto: invalid` + `X-Forwarded-Protocol: https` => Scheme() == "https"
  * `X-Forwarded-Proto: invalid` + `X-Forwarded-Protocol: invalid` + `X-Forwarded-Ssl: off` + `X-Url-Scheme: invalid` => Scheme() == "http"
  * `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` => "https"; `X-Forwarded-Protocol: http` => "http"; `X-Forwarded-Ssl: on` => "https"; `X-Url-Scheme: https` => "https"; no headers => "http"; TLS request => "https".
  Run `cd /echo && go test . -run TestZZTmpScheme -v` and report output. THEN DELETE /echo/context_zz_tmp_test.go.

ALSO: report `cd /echo && git status --porcelain` and `cd /echo && git stash list` and `cd /echo && git diff --stat`. If there is a leftover stash entry or any unexpected modification besides middleware/proxy.go and context.go, report it (do NOT drop the stash or revert anything; just report).

Report: the exact `git diff -- context.go`, the test output, confirmation the temp test file was deleted, and the git status/stash info.

You are working in a Go repository checked out at /echo (module github.com/labstack/echo/v4, go1.16 toolchain). FIX a bug in /echo/bind.go: binding form/query data into a `map[string][]string` destination PANICS (`reflect.Value.SetMapIndex: value of type string is not assignable to type []string`) because `bindData`'s map branch always stores `v[0]`.

Apply this fix to /echo/bind.go (change nothing else; do NOT touch any *_test.go file):

1) In `func (b *DefaultBinder) bindData(destination interface{}, data map[string][]string, tag string) error`, replace the map branch:
```go
	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		for k, v := range data {
			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
		}
		return nil
	}
```
with:
```go
	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		return b.bindDataToMap(destination, data)
	}
```

2) Add these new functions at the end of /echo/bind.go (after the last function in the file), keeping the file gofmt-clean:
```go
// bindDataToMap binds data into a map destination. Supported destinations are
// map[string][]string (all values of a key are bound), map[string]string and
// map[string]interface{} (only the first value of a key is bound).
func (b *DefaultBinder) bindDataToMap(destination interface{}, data map[string][]string) error {
	return bindDataToMap(destination, data)
}

func bindDataToMap(destination interface{}, data map[string][]string) error {
	val := reflect.ValueOf(destination).Elem()
	typ := val.Type()

	if typ.Kind() != reflect.Map {
		return errors.New("binding element must be a map")
	}
	if typ.Key().Kind() != reflect.String {
		return errors.New("map key must be a string")
	}
	if val.IsNil() {
		val.Set(reflect.MakeMap(typ))
	}

	switch typ.Elem().Kind() {
	case reflect.String:
		for k, v := range data {
			if len(v) == 0 {
				continue
			}
			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k).Convert(typ.Key()), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]).Convert(typ.Elem()))
		}
	case reflect.Slice:
		if typ.Elem().Elem().Kind() != reflect.String {
			return errors.New("map value must be a string slice")
		}
		for k, v := range data {
			slice := reflect.MakeSlice(typ.Elem(), len(v), len(v))
			for i := 0; i < len(v); i++ {
				slice.Index(i).SetString(v[i])
			}
			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k).Convert(typ.Key()), slice)
		}
	case reflect.Interface:
		for k, v := range data {
			if len(v) == 0 {
				continue
			}
			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k).Convert(typ.Key()), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
		}
	default:
		return errors.New("unsupported map type")
	}
	return nil
}
```
(Note: `bindDataToMap` must exist BOTH as a `*DefaultBinder` method and as a package-level function, as written above.)

Then verify:
- `cd /echo && gofmt -l bind.go` (nothing) and `cd /echo && go build ./...` and `cd /echo && go vet ./...`
- `cd /echo && go test -count=1 ./... 2>&1 | tail -20` — ALL pre-existing tests must still pass.
- Create a TEMPORARY test file /echo/zz_tmp_bind_test.go in package echo that checks: `new(DefaultBinder).bindData(&map[string][]string{}, map[string][]string{"a":{"1","2"},"b":{"3"}}, "form")` yields `map[string][]string{"a":{"1","2"},"b":{"3"}}`; `map[string]string` yields first values; `map[string]interface{}` yields first values; a nil `map[string][]string` destination gets filled; a form POST body `a=1&a=2&b=3` bound via `c.Bind(&map[string][]string{})` yields the multi-value map; and a query GET `?a=1&a=2&b=3` likewise. Run `cd /echo && go test . -run TestZZTmpBind -v` and report the output. THEN DELETE /echo/zz_tmp_bind_test.go.

Report concisely: the `git diff -- bind.go` stat, the temp test output, confirmation the temp file was deleted, and the final `go test -count=1 ./...` result.
